        "638366": {
         "recordId": "638366",
         "athleteName": "Jaylen Waddle",
         "positionAbbr": "WR",
         "teamId": "7",
         "teamAbbr": "DEN",
         "teamName": "Denver Broncos",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-22T07:21:27.433Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-23T02:32:38.541Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T01:01Z|Waddle brought in eight of 10 targets for 138 yards in the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T01:01Z",
           "shortComment": "Waddle brought in eight of 10 targets for 138 yards in the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "After a completely non-descript Broncos debut in Week 1, Waddle bounced back with a signature performance in Denver's come-from-behind victory. The veteran wideout led his team in all of receptions, receiving yards and targets by a wide margin, and the highlight of his afternoon was a spectacular 49-yard contested catch early in the second quarter that took the ball down to the Jaguars' one-yard line. The caliber of performance was emblematic of why the Broncos traded for Waddle this offseason, and it may serve as a launchpad for his role in the offense moving forward."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638407": {
         "recordId": "638407",
         "athleteName": "Courtland Sutton",
         "positionAbbr": "WR",
         "teamId": "7",
         "teamAbbr": "DEN",
         "teamName": "Denver Broncos",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-22T07:21:27.433Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-23T02:32:38.541Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T03:19Z|Sutton secured three of four targets for 25 yards in the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T03:19Z",
           "shortComment": "Sutton secured three of four targets for 25 yards in the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Sutton saw Jaylen Waddle spearhead the Broncos' air attack with an eight-catch, 138-yard day on 10 targets, while the former posted his second straight underwhelming line to open the season. Sutton has seen a modest nine targets over his first two games, and it remains to be seen if Waddle is in the early stages of taking over the No. 1 role in the team's passing attack. Sutton will look to make more of an impact in a Week 3 home showdown against the Rams next Sunday night."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638408": {
         "recordId": "638408",
         "athleteName": "Bo Nix",
         "positionAbbr": "QB",
         "teamId": "7",
         "teamAbbr": "DEN",
         "teamName": "Denver Broncos",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-22T07:21:27.433Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-23T02:32:38.541Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T03:24Z|Nix completed 22 of 31 passes for 288 yards with one touchdown and one interception while adding five carries for six yards in the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T03:24Z",
           "shortComment": "Nix completed 22 of 31 passes for 288 yards with one touchdown and one interception while adding five carries for six yards in the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Nix and the Broncos' offense started the game off in worrisome fashion, seemingly carrying over the malaise of their Week 1 Monday night loss to the Chiefs. Denver was still facing a 13-6 deficit heading into the fourth quarter, but Nix rallied the troops with a seven-yard touchdown pass to Nate Adkins and a key 17-yard strike to Evan Engram midway through the fourth quarter on what turned out to be the game-winning drive. The victory pulled the Broncos to 1-1 and gave Nix's early-season stats a serious boost heading into a Week 3 home showdown against the Rams next Sunday night."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638410": {
         "recordId": "638410",
         "athleteName": "Jonah Coleman",
         "positionAbbr": "RB",
         "teamId": "7",
         "teamAbbr": "DEN",
         "teamName": "Denver Broncos",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-22T07:21:27.433Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-23T02:32:38.541Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T03:29Z|Coleman rushed 10 times for 39 yards and a touchdown and brought in all three targets for 19 yards in the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T03:29Z",
           "shortComment": "Coleman rushed 10 times for 39 yards and a touchdown and brought in all three targets for 19 yards in the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "RJ Harvey (hamstring) was inactive and J.K. Dobbins exited the game with a hamstring injury of his own, opening the door for Coleman to enjoy an expanded role in his only his second NFL regular-season game. The rookie fourth-round pick also scored what turned out to be game-winning touchdown on a three-yard run just past the midway point of the fourth quarter, and he could be in line for a robust workload once again in a Week 3 interconference matchup against the Rams next Sunday night if either or both of Harvey and Dobbins are unavailable."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638446": {
         "recordId": "638446",
         "athleteName": "J.K. Dobbins",
         "positionAbbr": "RB",
         "teamId": "7",
         "teamAbbr": "DEN",
         "teamName": "Denver Broncos",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-22T07:21:27.433Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-23T02:32:38.541Z",
           "fp": "Questionable|2026-09-21T17:00Z|The Broncos believe that Dobbins' injured hamstring is \"good\" heading into next Sunday's game against the Rams, Tom Pelissero of Netflix reports.",
           "status": "Questionable",
           "date": "2026-09-21T17:00Z",
           "shortComment": "The Broncos believe that Dobbins' injured hamstring is \"good\" heading into next Sunday's game against the Rams, Tom Pelissero of Netflix reports.",
           "longComment": "The latest news on Dobbins aligns with what James Palmer of Bleacher Report previously relayed following the Broncos' 20-13 win over the Jaguars on Sunday, when Dobbins made an early exit due to a \"slight\" hamstring issue. While the Broncos are optimistic that Dobbins won't have to miss any time, his activity during practices Wednesday through Friday will ultimately determine whether he suits up against the Rams. Denver could have all of its key backfield members available for Week 3, as head coach Sean Payton suggested during his press conference Monday that RJ Harvey (hamstring) could return to action after sitting out against the Jaguars, per Nick Kosmider of The Athletic."
          }
         ]
        },
