           "date": "2026-09-21T23:29Z",
           "shortComment": "Cowboys head coach Brian Schottenheimer said S P.J. Locke (foot) could need a \"few weeks\" to recover after exiting Sunday's 37-20 win over the Commanders, Todd Archer of ESPN.com reports.",
           "longComment": "Schottenheimer revealed that Locke tore his plantar fascia in his right foot, which looks set to keep him sidelined for at least the Cowboys' Week 3 matchup with the Ravens in Brazil. With Locke out and Malik Hooker on the mend from a forearm injury, the Cowboys' depth at safety is already being tested early in the season."
