        "638241": {
         "recordId": "638241",
         "athleteName": "Bijan Robinson",
         "positionAbbr": "RB",
         "teamId": "1",
         "teamAbbr": "ATL",
         "teamName": "Atlanta Falcons",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-20T20:45Z|Robinson rushed 16 times for 72 yards and brought in three of four targets for nine yards in the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-20T20:45Z",
           "shortComment": "Robinson rushed 16 times for 72 yards and brought in three of four targets for nine yards in the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Considering the Falcons' air attack posed next to no threat to the Panthers defense while being helmed by Cooper Rush and Jack Strand, Robinson managed to put together a serviceable, albeit scoreless, day. The ultra-talented back didn't have a robust enough opportunity on the ground thanks to a game script that increasingly turned against the run, but Robinson's 4.5 yards per carry was more than respectable considering the circumstances. Either Michael Penix (knee) or Tua Tagovailoa (oblique) appear to have a chance to return for Thursday's Week 3 road matchup against the Packers, a development that would theoretically offer Robinson the opportunity to see some less crowded defensive fronts."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638258": {
         "recordId": "638258",
         "athleteName": "Drake London",
         "positionAbbr": "WR",
         "teamId": "1",
         "teamAbbr": "ATL",
         "teamName": "Atlanta Falcons",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-20T21:14Z|London brought in four of five targets for 51 yards and rushed once for minus-2 yards in the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-20T21:14Z",
           "shortComment": "London brought in four of five targets for 51 yards and rushed once for minus-2 yards in the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "London's reception, receiving yardage and target totals, modest as they were, all led the Falcons on an afternoon where Cooper Rush and Jack Strand combined to throw for 145 yards and toss three interceptions. Sunday's production pushed London's early-season line to 6-80-0 on 10 targets, but those numbers could be due for a nice boost as soon as Thursday's Week 3 road matchup against the Packers if either Michael Penix (knee) or Tua Tagovailoa (oblique) is deemed available for that contest."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638287": {
         "recordId": "638287",
         "athleteName": "Kyle Pitts Sr.",
         "positionAbbr": "TE",
         "teamId": "1",
         "teamAbbr": "ATL",
         "teamName": "Atlanta Falcons",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-20T22:02Z|Pitts brought in one of three targets for 15 yards in the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-20T22:02Z",
           "shortComment": "Pitts brought in one of three targets for 15 yards in the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Pitts was able to make his mark in the catch column for the first time in the new season, but that one reception turned out to be his only contribution on the afternoon. However, given Cooper Rush and Jack Strand combined to throw for only 145 yards and three interceptions, Pitts' sparse production is largely explained away. The talented tight end figures to see his outlook brighten whenever Michael Penix (knee) or Tua Tagovailoa (oblique) are able to suit up, with a Week 3 Thursday night road matchup against the Packers their next opportunity to do so."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638293": {
         "recordId": "638293",
         "athleteName": "Cooper Rush",
         "positionAbbr": "QB",
         "teamId": "1",
         "teamAbbr": "ATL",
         "teamName": "Atlanta Falcons",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-20T22:16Z|Rush completed 10 of 17 passes for 86 yards with no touchdowns and two interceptions while rushing twice for 20 yards before being benched in the third quarter of the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-20T22:16Z",
           "shortComment": "Rush completed 10 of 17 passes for 86 yards with no touchdowns and two interceptions while rushing twice for 20 yards before being benched in the third quarter of the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Rush's afternoon was about as difficult as his numbers suggest, and after he tossed his second interception of the day with 7:13 remaining in the third quarter, the veteran quarterback's day was done. Rookie replacement Jack Strand wasn't any better and tossed a pick-six during his time in the game, but if either Michael Penix (knee) or Tua Tagovailoa (oblique) is able to suit up for Thursday's Week 3 road matchup against the Packers, Rush may not necessarily be a shoo-in for No. 2 quarterback duties over his first-year teammate."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638383": {
         "recordId": "638383",
         "athleteName": "Jack Strand",
         "positionAbbr": "QB",
         "teamId": "1",
         "teamAbbr": "ATL",
         "teamName": "Atlanta Falcons",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T01:41Z|Strand completed just eight of 15 passes for 59 yards and an interception in the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T01:41Z",
           "shortComment": "Strand completed just eight of 15 passes for 59 yards and an interception in the Falcons' 34-3 loss to the Panthers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Cooper Rush was benched after going 10-for-17 passing with no touchdowns and two interceptions. Strand came on in relief and was just as ineffective. The 22-year-old is an undrafted rookie who played his college football at tiny Minnesota State-Moorhead, so it's no surprise he wasn't ready for the NFL in his first regular-season game action. With Michael Penix (knee) potentially back for Thursday night's game at Green Bay, Strand will be a cut candidate. Strand would make more sense on the practice squad where he can learn in a no-stress environment."
          }
         ]
        },
