        "638629": {
         "recordId": "638629",
         "athleteName": "Zach Bako-Bewele",
         "positionAbbr": "OT",
         "teamId": "9",
         "teamAbbr": "GB",
         "teamName": "Green Bay Packers",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Out|2026-09-22T18:32Z|Bako-Bewele said he sustained a complete tear of his right patellar tendon in Sunday's 20-17 overtime win over the Jets and will undergo season-ending surgery Thursday, Matt Schneidman of The Athletic reports.",
           "status": "Out",
           "date": "2026-09-22T18:32Z",
           "shortComment": "Bako-Bewele said he sustained a complete tear of his right patellar tendon in Sunday's 20-17 overtime win over the Jets and will undergo season-ending surgery Thursday, Matt Schneidman of The Athletic reports.",
           "longComment": "Widely viewed as the Packers' top offensive lineman, Bako-Bewele will face a roughly nine-month recovery from surgery, which he previously required for the same knee after suffering a partial patellar tendon tear last December. Anthony Belton is expected to take over as the Packers' new starting right tackle in place of Bako-Bewele, who will eye a return to the field in Week 1 of the 2027 season."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638694": {
         "recordId": "638694",
         "athleteName": "Chris Brooks",
         "positionAbbr": "RB",
         "teamId": "9",
         "teamAbbr": "GB",
         "teamName": "Green Bay Packers",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-23T00:31Z|Brooks tallied four carries for 11 yards and caught one of two targets for 15 yards during Sunday's 20-17 overtime win versus the Jets.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-23T00:31Z",
           "shortComment": "Brooks tallied four carries for 11 yards and caught one of two targets for 15 yards during Sunday's 20-17 overtime win versus the Jets.",
           "longComment": "Brooks was on the field for 27 of the Packers' 59 offensive snaps Week 2, with Kaleb Johnson and MarShawn Lloyd each logging 16. However, Brooks ceded carries to both players, and he tied Lloyd with two targets. The 26-year-old has totaled 40 yards off 11 carries (3.6 YPC), adding one catch for 15 yards in his two regular-season appearances in 2026. While Josh Jacobs (personal) sits on the Commissioner's Exempt List, there will continue to be opportunities for Brooks, Lloyd and Johnson, though it appears head coach Matt LaFleur is content with a timeshare, lowering the ceiling for all of them moving ahead, including the Week 3 meeting with Atlanta."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638702": {
         "recordId": "638702",
         "athleteName": "Jonnu Smith",
         "positionAbbr": "TE",
         "teamId": "9",
         "teamAbbr": "GB",
         "teamName": "Green Bay Packers",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-23T00:41Z|Smith played 13 of the Packers' 59 snaps during Sunday's 20-17 overtime win against the Jets.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-23T00:41Z",
           "shortComment": "Smith played 13 of the Packers' 59 snaps during Sunday's 20-17 overtime win against the Jets.",
           "longComment": "Smith was targeted three times in Green Bay's loss in Week 1, but he saw fewer snaps (13) at tight end in Week 2 than recent trade acquisition Mark Redman (20). Smith is still probably more likely to draw a target on any given snap than the in-line specialist Redman, but the former's snap share will be worth watching in Week 3 versus the Falcons."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638704": {
         "recordId": "638704",
         "athleteName": "Kaleb Johnson",
         "positionAbbr": "RB",
         "teamId": "9",
         "teamAbbr": "GB",
         "teamName": "Green Bay Packers",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-23T00:46Z|Johnson compiled eight carries for 32 yards during Sunday's 20-17 overtime win versus the Jets.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-23T00:46Z",
           "shortComment": "Johnson compiled eight carries for 32 yards during Sunday's 20-17 overtime win versus the Jets.",
           "longComment": "Johnson appeared in 16 of the Packers' 59 offensive snaps against the Jets, ending behind Chris Brooks (27) and tying with starter MarShawn Lloyd (16). However, none of them could get anything going, with all three players combining for 63 yards off 18 attempts. Johnson had plenty of hype entering his rookie season with the Steelers in 2025, though he wasn't very involved. With Josh Jacobs (personal) on the Commissioner's Exempt List, there will be snaps up for grabs. While that could mean more involvement from Johnson moving ahead, it seems as if head coach Matt LaFleur will continue to have all three players split carries, which isn't good news for fantasy managers, especially those looking to fill the void left by Jacobs' absence."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638717": {
         "recordId": "638717",
         "athleteName": "Skyy Moore",
         "positionAbbr": "WR",
         "teamId": "9",
         "teamAbbr": "GB",
         "teamName": "Green Bay Packers",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-23T01:15Z|Moore caught two of three targets for six yards during Sunday's 20-17 overtime win versus the Jets.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-23T01:15Z",
           "shortComment": "Moore caught two of three targets for six yards during Sunday's 20-17 overtime win versus the Jets.",
           "longComment": "Moore logged just four snaps in the 39-22 loss to the Vikings in Week 1, though it was a different story in Week 2, with the wideout appearing in 21 of the Packers' 59 offensive snaps against the Jets, finishing behind Christian Watson (53) and Matthew Golden (51) after Jayden Reed (back) lasted just two offensive plays. However, despite the increased workload, Moore didn't do anything meaningful for fantasy managers. That's not expected to change anytime soon, even if Watson or Golden aren't available at some point moving ahead."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638837": {
         "recordId": "638837",
         "athleteName": "Jayden Reed",
         "positionAbbr": "WR",
         "teamId": "9",
         "teamAbbr": "GB",
         "teamName": "Green Bay Packers",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-24T07:56:55.884Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-24T21:55:35.950Z",
           "fp": "Out|2026-09-23T20:13Z|Reed (neck) has been ruled out for Thursday's game against the Falcons, Wes Hodkiewicz of the Packers' official site reports.",
           "status": "Out",
           "date": "2026-09-23T20:13Z",
           "shortComment": "Reed (neck) has been ruled out for Thursday's game against the Falcons, Wes Hodkiewicz of the Packers' official site reports.",
           "longComment": "This was merely a formality after Reed was placed on a backboard and carted off the field after the Packers' second offensive play of this past Sunday's 20-17 overtime win at the Jets. He remained in the New York area afterward for further evaluation, and upon Reed's return to Green Bay on Tuesday, coach Matt LaFleur told Rob Demovsky of ESPN.com that the wide receiver's injury was contained to his neck area, and it's \"way too early\" to tell if he has a chance to play again this season until he undergoes additional medical tests. Christian Watson, Matthew Golden, Skyy Moore, Bo Melton and J. Michael Sturdivant will man the team's receiving corps Week 3 and beyond."
          }
         ]
        },
